# Story firmware caches (run_story_hardware.py applies this by default; --default-caches opts out).
# The board A/B that chose them (story Glimmer decode, dual core, 6 MB PSRAM staging):
#   IDF default, 16 KB ICache / 32 KB DCache, 32 B lines : 141 ms/token (timing build)
#   64 KB DCache, 64 B lines                              : 119 ms/token (timing build)
#   + 32 KB ICache (this file), display ON, plain build   : 106 -> 97 ms/token, golden MATCH
# A decode token streams ~5 MB of weights through the data cache, so its size and line
# length matter; the bigger instruction cache keeps the decode loop's code resident.
# The ICache's 16 KB of SRAM come out of the internal heap; the story's cold .bss and
# LVGL's heap live in PSRAM (sdkconfig.story.defaults, 65 KB), so the 147 KB KV cache
# stays internal either way (boot: 250 KB internal free with this file, display on).
CONFIG_ESP32S3_DATA_CACHE_64KB=y
CONFIG_ESP32S3_DATA_CACHE_8WAYS=y
CONFIG_ESP32S3_DATA_CACHE_LINE_64B=y
CONFIG_ESP32S3_INSTRUCTION_CACHE_32KB=y
CONFIG_ESP32S3_INSTRUCTION_CACHE_8WAYS=y
CONFIG_ESP32S3_INSTRUCTION_CACHE_LINE_32B=y
